/*=============================================================================

  Abs:  Functions for system monitoring and control.

  Name: subSys.c      
	   subSysinit      - general initialization
	   subSysFreqOff  - Cavity Frequency Offset Estimation
	   subSysFreqOAvg - Average Cavity Frequency Offset
	   subSysFreqErr  - Cavity Park Frequency Error Calculation
	   subSysPhaseTot - Direct Loop Phase Calculation
	   subSysPhaseCmb - Comb   Loop Phase Calculation
	   subSysPhaseStn - Station     Phase Calculation
	   subSysDCcoeff  - Ripple Loop DC Coefficient Calculation
	   subSysDrivSel  - Drive Power Setpoint Selection
	   subSysLog      - Value from Log Calculation
           subSysABreset  - Allen-Bradley reset

  Proto: not required and not used.  All functions called by the
         subroutine record get passed one argument:

         psub                       Pointer to the subroutine record data.
          Use:  pointer               In general, all functions read the
          Type: struct subRecord *    input fields (a to l) and write to
          Acc:  read/write            the val field.
          Mech: reference

         All functions return a long integer.  0 = OK, -1 = ERROR.
         The subroutine record ignores the status returned by the Init
         routines.  For the calculation routines, the record status (STAT) is
         set to SOFT_ALARM (unless it is already set to LINK_ALARM due to
         severity maximization) and the severity (SEVR) is set to psub->brsv
         (BRSV - set by the user in the database though it is expected to
          be invalid).

  Auth: 16-Jan-1997, Stephanie Allison
  Rev:  DD-MMM-YYYY, Reviewer's Name (.NE. Author's Name)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Mod:  
        07-Mar-2005, M. Laznovky -- added subSysABreset(), for EPICS 3.14.6
        02-Aug-2001, Stephanie Allison
        Add subroutines for average frequency offset and comb loop phase.
        28-Sep-2000, Stephanie Allison
        Make initial DC coeff for ripple loop gain tracking be enterable.

=============================================================================*/

